style-v2-agent-activity-across-thread-views

Lane: draft

FlatPatch: style-v2-agent-activity-across-thread-views

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema-snapshot

Purpose: Present consistent themed multi-agent v2 activity and root-relative contextual footer labels across live output and history replay without changing agent execution.

Requires: Unit:frontend/style-conversation-surfaces-with-theme

Provides: Capture explicit role model and effort constraints from their existing parse, compare them with the native effective startup snapshot using native effort normalization, and carry the optional display role through existing agent metadata and canonical activity items. Render Started, Interacted, Interrupted and Completed rows through one shared renderer for live and retained thread views, using uppercase underscore-separated path components with slash-separated ancestry and upstream description colors. Render white brackets around a capitalized explicit role in the active theme color, using red only for an observed model or effort mismatch. Omit the badge when the activity has no explicit role observation, including manual invocations and older replay records. Hide the v2 root footer label while retaining uppercase child labels even for a lone child view. Preserve native deferred activity FIFO order, streaming completion and prompt isolation.

Boundary: Own display observations and v2 presentation across thread views. Preserve native role and model precedence, effective effort resolution, configuration effects, agent membership, input admission, completion delivery and model-facing tool output. Reuse existing agent metadata and canonical activity owners without a second registry, render-time reads or stored-metadata backfill. Preserve v1 labels and picker presentation. Keep the formal prefix independent of this draft responsibility.

Verification: Native role-creation and startup-effort checks cover explicit roles, omitted roles, effective alias resolution, mismatch reporting and unchanged child settings. Canonical item, history and app-server conversion checks preserve optional role observations. TUI checks cover dark and light theme role colors, white brackets, red mismatches, uppercase root-relative labels and upstream description colors in live and retained views, absent badges without explicit roles, child ancestry and hidden v2 root labels while retaining v1 behavior. Streaming checks retain authoritative answers, interruption and late-completion behavior, prompt isolation and shared live and replay presentation in FIFO order.


